  description: 'The Zapotec state of the Valley of Oaxaca, ruled from the levelled mountaintop city of Monte Albán, founded about 500 BCE. It conquered outlying valleys in the last centuries BCE, peaked in the Classic (about 200–700 CE) with ties to Teotihuacan, and was largely abandoned by about 850.',
  timelineItemIds: ['mx-monte-alban'],
  confidence: conf('conjectural', 'Monte Albán’s phases are well dated and its conquest slabs name subject places, but its borders are unknown. The outline is central Oaxaca (the Valley of Oaxaca and the northern sierra), which includes the Cuicatlán Cañada it ruled in Monte Albán II.'),
  sources: [W('Monte Albán'), W('Zapotec civilization')],
